            <ArticleTitle>Forbidden suffering: the Pollyanna syndrome of the disabled and their families.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>431-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Has suffering become an ugly word in the normalization debate? Are the disabled and their families forced into a Pollyanna culture in order to be acknowledged and accepted in good company as the worthy disabled? This essay poses a controversial question: I would like to start a debate and ask whether normalization also has an unseen, ideological downside.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
